{"id":"n-20261007-u9tpm9","category":"sports","display_title":"Kerem Primo Reaches Judo Final","display_title_he":"כרם פרימו העפילה לגמר הג'ודו","short_summary":"Israeli judoka Kerem Primo secured at least a silver medal by advancing to the final of the World Judo Championships in Baku.","english_level":"C1","words":421,"reading_time":3,"image":null,"sources":[{"name":"Ynet","domain":"ynet.co.il","url":"https://www.ynet.co.il/sport/article/bj7cnc7sgx","title":"הישג מרשים: כרם פרימו העפילה לגמר אליפות העולם בג'ודו","published_at":"2026-10-07T11:37:18.000Z"},{"name":"Walla","domain":"sports.walla.co.il","url":"https://sports.walla.co.il/item/3871236","title":"יש מדליה! כרם פרימו בגמר אליפות העולם בג'ודו","published_at":"2026-10-07T10:47:00.000Z"}],"published_at":"2026-10-07T10:47:00.000Z","first_published_in_app_at":"2026-10-07T13:52:21.279Z","quality_score":9,"interest_score":8,"verification_status":"verified","content_status":"published","paragraphs":["The World Judo Championships in Baku witnessed a remarkable milestone for the Israeli delegation as twenty-one-year-old Kerem Primo fought her way through a fiercely competitive bracket to secure a spot in the final. Competing in the under-63 kg weight category, the twenty-seventh-ranked athlete guaranteed herself at least a silver medal, marking a career-defining achievement on the international stage. Her impressive run provided a much-needed highlight for the national team following several early exits by her compatriots earlier in the tournament, occurring on a day that also marked three years since the October 7 massacre.","Primo began her campaign with a compelling victory over Italy's Carlotta Avanzato, demonstrating dominance before finishing the contest with a decisive hold-down following an early waza-ari. Her second match presented a severe test against Poland's Angelika Szymanska, a formidable opponent who is ranked seventh in the world and serves as the 2024 world silver medalist. Despite falling behind on points due to her opponent's yuko and waza-ari, and accumulating penalties, Primo capitalized on her opponent's late mistakes to snatch a dramatic victory when Szymanska received a third penalty. She continued her momentum in the round of sixteen by overcoming Australia's Maeve Coughlan, a twenty-seven-year-old reigning Oceania champion, with a strategic yuko score.","The quarterfinal clash brought an even greater challenge against Mongolia's Enkhriilen Lkhagvatogoo, the second-ranked judoka in the world, whose resume includes two bronze medals from the 2022 and 2023 world championships. Undeterred by her opponent's stellar reputation, Primo secured an early waza-ari in the first minute and maintained her lead until the final bell, despite picking up a late penalty. In the semifinal, she faced Hungary's Anna Kriza, completing a dominant performance with an ippon after an early yuko to officially seal her place in the championship match. This performance stands out as a triumphant breakthrough for the young competitor, establishing her among the elite fighters in her division and securing the first medal for the Israeli delegation in Baku.","Looking ahead to the decisive battle for the gold, Primo is scheduled to face Japan's Haruka Kajio. As the reigning world champion who won gold in 2025, the Asian champion of the same year, and the top-ranked athlete globally with five Grand Slam titles, Kajio represents the ultimate test for the rising Israeli star. While other members of the national delegation, including Yonatan Albaz who finished fifth after reaching the quarterfinals, continue to navigate challenging bouts and upcoming recoveries like Inbar Lanir, all attention in the sport is now focused on Primo's pursuit of the ultimate world title in Baku."],"facts":[{"fact":"Kerem Primo advanced to the final of the World Judo Championships in Baku in the under-63 kg category, guaranteeing at least a silver medal.","sources":[1,2]},{"fact":"Primo is 21 years old and ranked 27th in the world.","sources":[2]},{"fact":"On her way to the final, Primo defeated Carlotta Avanzato, Angelika Szymanska, Maeve Coughlan, Enkhriilen Lkhagvatogoo, and Anna Kriza.","sources":[1,2]},{"fact":"In the final, Primo is set to face Japanese judoka Haruka Kajio, who is ranked first in the world and is the reigning world champion.","sources":[1,2]},{"fact":"This achievement marks the first medal for the Israeli delegation at the tournament in Baku.","sources":[1,2]},{"fact":"Other Israeli delegation members, including Gefen Primo and Yonatan Albaz, experienced early exits or missed out on medals.","sources":[1]}],"glossary":[{"text":"World Judo Championships","lemma":"World Judo Championships","pos":"noun","he":"אליפות העולם בג'ודו","name":true},{"text":"Baku","lemma":"Baku","pos":"noun","he":"באקו","name":true},{"text":"witnessed","lemma":"witness","pos":"verb","he":"חזה ב","name":false},{"text":"remarkable","lemma":"remarkable","pos":"adjective","he":"מרשים","name":false},{"text":"milestone","lemma":"milestone","pos":"noun","he":"אבן דרך","name":false},{"text":"Israeli","lemma":"Israeli","pos":"adjective","he":"ישראלי","name":true},{"text":"delegation","lemma":"delegation","pos":"noun","he":"משלחת","name":false},{"text":"Kerem Primo","lemma":"Kerem Primo","pos":"noun","he":"כרם פרימו","name":true},{"text":"fought","lemma":"fight","pos":"verb","he":"נלחם","name":false},{"text":"fiercely","lemma":"fiercely","pos":"adverb","he":"באופן קשוח","name":false},{"text":"competitive","lemma":"competitive","pos":"adjective","he":"תחרותי","name":false},{"text":"bracket","lemma":"bracket","pos":"noun","he":"טבלת טורניר","name":false},{"text":"secure","lemma":"secure","pos":"verb","he":"להבטיח","name":false},{"text":"spot","lemma":"spot","pos":"noun","he":"מקום","name":false},{"text":"final","lemma":"final","pos":"noun","he":"גמר","name":false},{"text":"competing","lemma":"compete","pos":"verb","he":"מתחרה","name":false},{"text":"weight","lemma":"weight","pos":"noun